{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1355554-example-on-how-mages-discard-their-foci","id":1355554,"title":"Example on how Mages discard their foci.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-17T19:05:11-08:00","id":1355554,"title":"Example on how Mages discard their foci.","content":"In order to draw a straight line on a piece of paper you need 3 things: A sheet of paper, a ruler and a pen.<br /> <br /> At arete 3 you use all 3 of these foci to accomplish your magick. The paper, the ruler and the pen.<br /> <br /> At arete 4 you realize that you don't need a ruler, you can draw perfect straight lines just fine without it, but it's definitely easier with the additional tool (-1 difficulty).<br /> <br /> At arete 5 you discard the paper. Only one foci remaining.<br /> <br /> At arete 6 you don't even need a pen anymore. Now you can draw straight lines on a piece of paper out of sheer force of will.<br /> <br /> This example is meant to emphasize how difficult it is to discard your tools, how can you possibly draw straight lines on a piece of paper without the paper to begin with? The ruler is easy enough to discard, but the other two? <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12475-junioralr","name":"JuniorALR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12475_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T02:16:41-08:00","id":1355604,"title":"","content":"Draw it in the air with your imagination, and really truly believe it is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T03:50:28-08:00","id":1355608,"title":"","content":"I don't think your analogy quite works. Let me try to present you with a more accurate one:<br /> <br /> Your mage has<br /> * pencil/eraser for making drawings on paper<br /> * Oil colors for making oil drawings on canvas<br /> * An airbrush to make art on cars<br /> * A 3d pen (look them up) for constructing fancy things in 3D<br /> <br /> Now, the Mage isn't that stoic - they know they could do airbrush on canvas, for example, but this is how they favorte setup is to do things.<br /> <br /> But! Enlightenment strikes! They realize that they don't *need* a pencil and eraser to do drawings! They understand the concept and creation of drawings in such a fundamental way, they can make them just appear! But painting on canvas? Airbrushing metallic surfaces? Oh no, that requires the tools still. Drawings are much simpler in concept after all, not really the same thing. Such a thing can be willed.<br /> <br /> Next enlightenment strikes! Oh what a fool that mage was! Of course you can create the airbrush art on metal without the tools! I mean, it's super *easy* now if they still use them - but they don't need to.<br /> <br /> Painting on canvas? Oh no. nono. The mixing of the colors. The preparation of the canvas with foundation. The careful selection of colors. Nono, this cannot be done without all those tools...<br /> ...and don't even talk about *3d painting* without a 3d pen, ha-ha that's just silly...<br /> <br /> ...surely. Right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-18-2019, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T03:51:01-08:00","id":1355609,"title":"","content":"I like your analogy Ambrosia, thanks. That's how I imagine it would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12475,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12475-junioralr","user":"JuniorALR","date":". 12-18-2019, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12475-junioralr","name":"JuniorALR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12475_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T12:05:26-08:00","id":1356341,"title":"","content":"I think the Sticker here is that it has to make sense to the Mage. Which is a Huge sticker when you consider the most people are unfortunately very rational.<br /> <br /> You probably can't have 2 &quot;Create image&quot; foci as different foci for the same mage because of how similar the creation process is. If you can manifest ink on paper with your mind alone, wouldn't a rational person start to question why they'd need a paintbrush to paint?<br /> <br /> Heck why do you need paper? If you can move things with your mind, why not just spread the pigments the way you imagine onto any surface you can see. Why couldn't you sculpt?<br /> <br /> In this case, a mage with an &quot;Artistic&quot; paradigm might start to question their own paradigm if the started to not need their tools, the tools are integral to the paradigm. You loose one and the artist may come to the reasonable(from their perspective) conclusion that their raw creativity has manifested in some form of telekinesis.<br /> <br /> In this case I'd say it'd be reasonable for the player to drop 1 focus and change the form that the other 2 foci take to fit with the character's paradigm shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}